    "title": {
     "en": "Ikra and Samina"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "Ikra and her sister Samina had one sheet of drawing paper. Ikra offered half of the paper or two quarters. Samina chose two quarters."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "half",
     "quarter",
     "equal parts",
     "fraction"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "Ikra and her little sister Samina decide to draw but have only one sheet. Ikra wants to divide it in half, but Samina wants a bigger part.\nIkra asks: would you like half of the paper, or two quarters? Samina thinks two quarters sounds bigger and chooses it.\nBoth are the same! Two quarters make a half, so Ikra shared the paper equally.\nWhen an object is divided into two equal parts, each part is a half, written 1/2.\nWhen divided into four equal parts, each part is a quarter, written 1/4.\nThe parts must be equal. Try it with a paper by folding."
    }
